;; The net/http corpus's non-passes before net/http is listed (doc/go/NET-HTTP-SURVEY.md, "As built: NH1",
;; "As built: NH11 (b)"): the classes every program of bin/goi check --corpus nethttp that does not pass
;; falls into, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format (a program's class is the first whose :match finds
;; "RESULT REASON", and whose :programs, when given, name it; bin/goi divergences --nethttp checks the
;; reference test/nethttp/check-linux-amd64.edn against them, test/goi/divergences.ae). net/http is
;; interpreted from its embedded forms, as GR8a made it importable. NH1's four classes went with NH11 (b)
;; (the empty method sets, the stub slots, and the resets and the hang they caused). The classes left are
;; :deferred: NH2 (a) lists net/http, its sub-packages and their dependencies compiled, and NH3 runs the
;; corpus on the listed package; they then go, or the ones that remain are by design. Read with the
;; Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :first-request-slow
  :title "a deadline of 80 to 100 ms shorter than an interpreted net/http's first request"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the first request that runs a server path builds its functions (built on first call, S18) and interprets them: 177 to 353 ms for timeout_client's second GET, which its 100 ms Client.Timeout cuts (the nil response dereferenced); timeout_context's request does not reach the handler within its 80 ms, so the program waits on the handler's channel until the check's wall cap"
  :decided "NH11 (b); NH2 (a)"
  :programs ["timeout_client" "timeout_context"]
  :match [#"nil pointer dereference" #"^error timeout"]}
 {:id :split-internal
  :title "an interpreted net/http/httptrace's internal/nettrace is not compiled net's"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "httptrace installs its dial hooks under internal/nettrace's TraceKey; with httptrace interpreted that is an interpreted copy of internal/nettrace (unlisted), whose key type compiled net's Dialer does not look up, so ConnectStart and ConnectDone are never called"
  :decided "NH11 (b); NH2 (a)"
  :programs ["httptrace_events"]
  :match [#"^fail status 0 \(gc 0\), stdout differs$"]}
 {:id :caller-paths
  :title "runtime.Caller's file of an interpreted caller in net/http's messages"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "ServeMux's conflict message names where a pattern was registered (runtime.Caller); for an interpreted caller goi gives its forms' relative name, gc the source's absolute path (test/goi/divergences.edn's runtime.Caller class)"
  :decided "NH11 (b); NH2 (a) (the caller stays interpreted: by design then)"
  :programs ["mux_precedence"]
  :match [#"^fail status 0 \(gc 0\), stdout differs$"]}
]
